ght, Full, and Null Angles" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110864 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186111728 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110864 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048723 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110864 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110864 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "e304faa7-71b9-5828-9e54-310c7f686f0d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110922 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186107423 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110922 #edb/ref 1069 "q-150686" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110922 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110922 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following shows a right angle?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110922 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a35e2e91-fb74-51ab-adf6-759adba6c939" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186110922 #edb/ref 1074 "A right angle has a degree measure of ${90}^{∘}.$ This corresponds to one-quarter of a full turn.\n\nAmong the given options, the only right angle is the following:\n\n![](images/bc/bc5cc4627ba0cb06a7f38ccdfc1621dcdf55d431d637b43fbf5c5ad8c9229acd.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111240 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186109165 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111240 #edb/ref 1069 "q-52645" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111240 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111240 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following shows a full angle?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111240 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3514c695-c32e-544d-9691-01756c854550" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111240 #edb/ref 1074 "A full angle has a degree measure of ${360}^{∘}.$ This corresponds to a full turn.\n\nAmong the given options, the only full angle is the following:\n\n![](images/a5/a52ce1848c072141aa67b53b27546d1d725ed66b28254bd0f1a0eb29a27bc3f5.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111611 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111612 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111611 #edb/ref 1061 40054 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111611 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "46ebc539-57b3-5556-981c-c8b83bb8d7f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111611 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110672 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111612 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111746 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111612 #edb/ref 1061 40055 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111612 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a1fd3388-710f-5be2-bb9b-e0952aac5833" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111612 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110673 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111728 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186111611 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111728 #edb/ref 1061 8748 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111728 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "73c2d122-acf8-55a5-835f-6ae907dc910c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111728 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186111837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111746 #edb/ref 1061 8781 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111746 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "07919ee0-ec2e-550b-8146-bd88c640d46f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111746 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186110763 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111837 #edb/ref 1064 "Some angles have special names.\n\n- A **right angle** has a measure of $90^\\circ.$ It corresponds to one-quarter of a full turn.\n\n![](images/15/155a1d6d2abd868b05674dec47ef4b20a5147d30cd328a5ba53d00dea271d65c.png)\n\n- A **straight angle**, which is just a straight line, has a measure of $180^\\circ.$ It corresponds to one-half of a full turn.\n\n![](images/24/2423950f80de8354aee74c4f1daa6e42cf376caa0365307c76ebc7e09f96c8cf.png)\n\n- A **null angle** has a measure of $0^\\circ.$ You can imagine \"closing\" the angle until the two sides of the angle overlap. In this case, we don't have any turn, so its measure is zero!\n\n![](images/f8/f86b7c1b7ba758fb6b07b6aeabd03395d29103b45e4cd220444b675f70a6e630.png)\n\n- A **full angle** has a measure of $360^\\circ.$ You can imagine \"opening\" the angle until one of the sides goes all the way around. So, this is the angle between a ray and itself after it has made one full turn.\n\n![](images/cb/cbc9e288f4d3905357539a221954328ef0ac799531fab62f034364d32a7c0f29.png)\n\nOn a diagram, null and full angles can look the same, so it is up to us what we choose to call it." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111837 #edb/ref 1065 2178 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111837 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "74e7b6f4-d873-55dc-81f9-6bf4148828b1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186111837 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431189 #edb/ref 1080 "Full or Straight" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431189 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431189 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "00626d6e-47ea-5b73-ace3-c239ab797dda" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431190 #edb/ref 1080 "images/a3/a38e421522cda08a156c3423a623290dc7c6a4db165c3c7a243b85d4f462eae9.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431190 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431190 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "02ad844e-8c87-5c5d-b549-5103fa7c31de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431191 #edb/ref 1080 "images/fc/fc1014f6b5cb3dca17255a3be05c65491141c4c017ca48be5136b6be7b1b2095.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431191 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431191 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "091434ba-eb8d-5e07-a0f7-d8455360e6e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431192 #edb/ref 1080 "images/7a/7ac53ac9bc07fa744da0b0bc6499d1ebd7cfb0be92060f98003cce09060ad0e4.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431192 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431192 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "09283728-5c54-5155-b2ed-274340528061" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431193 #edb/ref 1080 "images/d0/d0076450a7583f48e9763eb845ec635cbff525b7c7605ab358bcfbfb9dc71514.png" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431193 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045497 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431193 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0a2b823b-5463-5d20-82db-4d5481b520f4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186431194 #edb/ref 1080 "images/f9/f97a65c209bc19c32